WEBVTT

00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:04.900
Enter the fray, king of all Knights!

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:07.270
I ride...

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:09.580
the King of Knights, Alfred!

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.610
I call the Solitary Knight, Gancelot!

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:17.490
The Little Sage, Marron!

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.620
The Yggdrasil Maiden, Elaine!

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:22.720
And the Knight of Truth, Gordon!

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.600
Thattaboy, Aichi!

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.750
He still had good cards left!

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:32.100
Well, the situation is not as optimistic as it seems.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:32.850
Eh?

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.610
Look at Aichi's hand.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.440
His hand...

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:38.500
He's got nothing!

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.210
Mm.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:43.570
He was driven to the point where 
he had to use up all his cards.

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:47.290
And even with that, Alfred's 
power is only 18000.

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:50.270
He wasn't able to reach full power...

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:53.990
To make matters worse, he just put 
Gordon into the deck this morning...

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:57.990
The deck that Brother's using now has 
never even been play-tested before!

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.860
It's a deck he just put together!

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:02.130
W-What?!

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:05.030
Nobody knows whether that deck...

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:06.890
...works well or not!

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:51.020
The Knight of Truth, Gordon...

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:08.970
This unit is a new card that I
 have just put into the deck,

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:12.580
With this card... No, not only Gordon.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:17.500
This new deck... How should I 
fight to reach its full potential...

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:24.330
What's wrong?

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:27.940
You thought about and chose 
that deck yourself, didn't you?

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:32.060
Right now, all you can do is believe in that.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.150
What's up?!

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:36.900
How long are you gonna keep me hangin' here?!

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.950
Or is your turn over?

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:43.020
N-Not yet.

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:44.620
Please wait just a little longer...

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:49.320
Don't tell me it's your first 
time at a tournament like this?

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:52.100
I see. No wonder...

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:56.830
The most important thing in a 
Vanguard fight is keeping your cool,

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:00.720
so, given the way he looks, they might as 
well declare me the winner right now...

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:09.260
New Allies

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:11.690
I'm sorry to have kept you waiting.

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:15.150
I attack with Gancelot, boosted by Marron.

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.020
I guard with Tahr!

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:28.550
Next, Alfred!

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:29.420
Let's go!

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.510
Twin drive check!

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:36.170
Yes!

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:37.270
There it is!

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:39.050
Critical trigger!

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:41.450
I add +5000 to the power of Gordon!

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:44.600
I give the extra critical to Alfred!

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:52.830
There you go! What about the damage trigger?

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:54.700
First card...

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:57.200
Second card...

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:58.310
No trigger!

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:00.950
All right! So that's 4 damage!

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:04.200
I attack with Gordon, boosted by Elaine!

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:06.320
I guard with Barri!

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:13.450
I drop Bahr to activate Barri's skill!

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:25.260
During this battle, this 
Kagero unit cannot be hit!

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:29.680
I can repel any number of 
namby-pamby attacks like that one.

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:32.430
My turn's over...

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:35.040
-Damn it!
-It's weird...

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:37.520
It's too weird... Snake...

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:39.730
You've got Yaksha, don't you?

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:41.090
Since it's grade 3...

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:44.470
The image I have and that one 
are a little different...

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:46.720
You don't have a strong imagination, do you?

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:47.930
NI, yo!

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:52.530
I'll show you what a real 
attack looks like...

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:54.780
I call Bahr!

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:02.720
I attack your Alfred with my 
Berserk Dragon, boosted by Joka!

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:06.720
No guard!

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:17.010
Let's go, Bahr! Give me a boost!

00:06:23.510 --> 00:06:26.550
Twin drive! Come on, trigger!

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:29.580
Critical trigger, activated!

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:33.300
I can't believe he really got one!

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:35.700
It's like he really is a magician!

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:37.090
Brother!

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:40.090
I add +5000 to the power of Tejas!

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:44.740
And I also add +1 critical!

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:48.260
Damage check!

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:49.570
First card...

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:51.650
Second card...

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:55.360
This isn't good! Now he's at 5 damage!

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:59.000
Even though his opponent's got 
another attack left with Tejas...

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:02.320
Aichi! Whatever you do, protect yourself!

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:05.690
I know, but...

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:09.280
Well, let's see what Aichi does.

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:14.340
This is the end of the line for you!

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:16.780
Tejas attacks Alfred!

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:20.860
Of course, Jarran boosts... and at 
the same time, he activates a skill.

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:23.750
Tejas's power is +4000!

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.620
I guard with Wingal!

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:32.770
No! He's still 8000 short!

00:07:32.770 --> 00:07:34.990
Aichi! One more card!

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:36.430
You need one more card!

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:39.920
Llew's shield is 10000...

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:43.980
If I use him to guard, I'd be 
able to block Tejas's attack.

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:44.760
But...

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:50.380
If I use Llew now, I won't have 
any cards left in my hand.

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:54.160
Isn't there some other way?

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:00.870
I've got it!

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:04.280
What are you doing, Aichi?! This 
is no time to be daydreaming!

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:06.370
For now, the unit from my hand...

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:07.740
will only be Wingal!

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:09.120
Whaaat?!

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:11.800
You're still rattled?

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.630
Can't you count how 
much damage you've taken?"

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:16.680
No, I'm calm now.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.000
What?!

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.570
This is the conclusion I've 
come to after thinking coolly.

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:23.190
The action I should take right now is...

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:26.010
Please, Gordon! Intercept!

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:32.350
Intercept, eh?

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:35.600
That's also quite an expected move.

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:40.630
When intercepting, that unit's 
shield is only 5000, I believe.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:45.040
You're still 3000 short.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:51.680
He's getting creamed!

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:53.890
This is the sixth damage!

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:06.510
I-I don't believe it!

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:08.400
Why didn't he take any damage?!

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:09.460
Yesss!

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:18.290
What?!

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:20.850
Why was his shield at 10000?!

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:23.510
Because it wasn't a regular interception.

00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:24.910
Say what?!

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:27.210
When Gordon intercepts...

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:31.870
if a Royal Paladin is in the
Vanguard circle, his shield gains +5000!

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:38.710
What is this?!

00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:43.220
It's an unshakable intercept that 
reliably ambushes the approaching enemy.

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:46.730
It's an Especial Intercept.

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:49.250
Especial Intercept?!

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:51.290
I've never seen that skill before!

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:53.440
It's the first time for me, too.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:54.260
Huh?!

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:59.320
See, the Knight of Truth, Gordon, is a card 
that I just put into my deck this morning.

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:02.520
You mean it's from 
"Onslaught of Dragon Souls"?!

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:03.620
That's right.

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:05.620
Wow!

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:09.030
Thank you, Gordon. You saved me.

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:13.630
I did not expect him to be able to use a 
"Onslaught of Dragon Souls" card already,

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:15.090
when they've just been released?!

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:17.720
I think I may have underestimated 
him a little...

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:20.180
That's the end of my turn!

00:10:20.410 --> 00:10:21.770
He did it.

00:10:21.770 --> 00:10:24.500
He withstood that attack brilliantly.

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:27.040
Damage 5...

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:28.980
I only have Llew in my hand.

00:10:29.470 --> 00:10:32.160
No matter what happens, I 
wanna settle it this turn!

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:42.160
I got it!

00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:44.610
I call Gigantech Charger!

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:51.260
I activate its skill!

00:10:51.260 --> 00:10:53.750
I open the card that's on top of the deck!

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:58.560
Since it's a Royal Paladin, 
I move it to the rear-guard!

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:02.680
Gigantech Charger?

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:04.950
I haven't seen that unit before, either.

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:08.760
More important is Flogal, which 
he brought out with that skill.

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:11.480
Huh? Even though it's grade 0?

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:14.730
As always, you're fixated 
on grades, Lose-umi.

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:15.930
That's right!

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:17.160
What?!

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:19.510
Look closely, Lose-umi.

00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:24.530
Because of Flogal, Brother Aichi's 
Alfred is up to full power.

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:30.940
That's another new card 
he's used effectively.

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:34.680
And now...

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:38.050
Here I go!

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:54.650
Here I go!

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:59.230
I attack with Gigantech Charger, 
boosted by Elaine!

00:12:15.220 --> 00:12:16.600
Trigger check!

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:19.430
Yes! No trigger!

00:12:22.330 --> 00:12:24.710
If the next attack hits...

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:26.580
Aichi wins it!

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:28.390
Okay, here I go!

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:33.300
I defend with Tahr!

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:37.050
And add Joka as well!

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:42.040
If I can just get through this turn, I win...

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:45.720
Twin drive, first check!

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:51.670
Second check!

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:57.880
He got it!

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:00.180
Critical trigger!

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:01.340
What?!

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:05.220
I give the power and the 
critical to Alfred!

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:08.800
N-No way!

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:17.370
Damage check...

00:13:18.510 --> 00:13:21.480
...No trigger.

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:29.160
The result of the first matchup 
of the first fight:

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:32.800
The winner is Aichi Sendou, from Team Q4.

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:42.300
Yeah!

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:49.190
I won...

00:13:49.190 --> 00:13:51.370
You did it, Brother!

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:53.320
Kamui!

00:13:53.320 --> 00:13:55.940
I knew you'd win!

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:56.810
Thank you.

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:58.030
Yeesh!

00:13:58.030 --> 00:13:59.760
You had us on the edge of our seats!

00:13:59.760 --> 00:14:03.020
Why didn't the other guy intercept?

00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:06.310
Oh, he did the right thing.

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:09.590
Those two units...

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:13.190
Certainly, if even one 
of them had intercepted,

00:14:13.190 --> 00:14:15.960
he would've been able to protect 
against Alfred's attack...

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:19.420
But Aichi still had Gancelot.

00:14:20.310 --> 00:14:23.440
So even if the guy had 
survived Alfred's attack,

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:28.600
against an attack from Gancelot, boosted 
by Marron, without any triggers in play,

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:30.890
he would've had no defense.

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:33.010
Then he...

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:34.390
Can you imagine it?

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:37.000
That guy annoys me...

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:40.640
Aichi, the moment you drew 
the critical trigger...

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:42.000
The outcome was decided.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:43.780
And there we go.

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:45.130
Good for you!

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:50.580
I suppose luck was on your side...

00:14:51.310 --> 00:14:55.060
But you had good command of a new deck...

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:56.640
and that made all the difference.

00:14:58.600 --> 00:15:02.080
And now, we continue with the second matchup.

00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:07.430
We have plenty of excitement in 
regional tournament halls across the nation.

00:15:07.430 --> 00:15:11.480
Now how about the contest here in Kanto 
Region 3?! Let me hear some noise!

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:21.360
The next fight is between 
Toshiki Kai and Laito Kurosaki!

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:27.950
Good luck, Kai!

00:15:27.950 --> 00:15:31.450
Make it two wins in a row, you hear me?!

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:33.580
I don't need to be told.

00:15:39.280 --> 00:15:42.130
Well, he doesn't need my advice to win.

00:15:42.130 --> 00:15:45.820
Oh, you admit it, Lose-umi!

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:48.070
Shut up! The name's Katsumi!

00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:51.510
Stand up, the Vanguard!

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:01.490
Huh. That guy uses Kagero, too.

00:16:01.490 --> 00:16:03.500
A fight between two players 
using the same deck...

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:05.020
This'll be a good one!

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:10.020
Interesting...

00:16:10.020 --> 00:16:13.780
This'll decide which of us 
is the real master of Kagero.

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:20.200
I hope you don't think you're gonna 
keep that composed expression!

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:27.400
I see... So the much-hyped team 
over there is advancing smoothly...

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:30.000
Oh, I'd say we're getting our 
share of excitement, too...

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:38.060
I-I don't believe it!

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:42.400
Y-You protected yourself completely against 
the fierce attack of my dragon army corps?!

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:53.010
You're all mouth.

00:16:54.100 --> 00:16:57.910
I'll teach you the real way to use a dragon.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.160
Counterblast!

00:17:02.210 --> 00:17:06.260
I destroy your Tejas with my 
Overlord, boosted by Bahr!

00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:08.890
Check!

00:17:10.310 --> 00:17:11.760
No trigger.

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:17.780
Overlord's attack hit me, which means...

00:17:17.780 --> 00:17:19.640
Right. He stands.

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:22.140
Ready? Next up is Goku.

00:17:23.550 --> 00:17:24.890
I guard with Ganlu!

00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:28.770
That's fine.

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:31.250
Check the drive trigger.

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:34.840
I got a critical trigger.

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:36.670
Power critical...

00:17:36.670 --> 00:17:38.280
to Overlord!

00:17:45.670 --> 00:17:46.500
C-Crap!

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:48.500
It stands yet again.

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:50.580
Time to finish you off...

00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:55.770
Oh, no... No guard!

00:17:56.190 --> 00:17:59.300
If I can only draw a heal trigger, 
there's still a chance...

00:17:59.630 --> 00:18:01.680
Check the drive trigger.

00:18:03.950 --> 00:18:05.950
Don't tell me...

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:08.170
Got it.

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:12.650
I give all the effects to Overlord.

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:21.410
I'm not dead yet! If I can 
draw two heal triggers...

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:22.530
First card...

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:24.790
Second card...

00:18:35.810 --> 00:18:37.420
The result of the second 
matchup of the first fight:

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:39.350
The winner, from Team Q4...

00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:40.720
Toshiki Kai!

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:48.230
So now we know that, when it comes to 
using Kagero, I am better than you.

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:52.190
Lucky bastard drew two criticals...

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:54.120
No, look closely!

00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:54.680
Hm?

00:18:54.680 --> 00:18:58.590
Kai still had two units left that 
he hadn't attacked with yet!

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:00.320
In other words...

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:05.310
even without the critical triggers, I'm 
pretty sure he would've won this turn.

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:06.290
Then...

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:07.800
Kai crushed him!

00:19:10.930 --> 00:19:12.290
Awesome...

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:14.250
Kai really is incredible!

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:19.490
He overwhelmed the guy, ka-boom!

00:19:19.490 --> 00:19:21.960
You know this Toshiki Kai?

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:22.830
Uh-uh...

00:19:22.830 --> 00:19:26.900
Unbelievable that a fighter like that could 
have stayed off the radar 'til now...

00:19:28.970 --> 00:19:30.450
I see...

00:19:30.450 --> 00:19:35.060
This is the team you turned 
Team Handsome down to join...

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:35.980
Kamui...

00:19:35.980 --> 00:19:37.730
Is something wrong?

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:40.740
Nope. I'm just lookin' forward to
 the Finals even more now.

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:42.830
Congratulations, Kai!

00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:45.800
If anyone could pull off an overwhelming 
victory at regionals, it's you!

00:19:45.800 --> 00:19:49.370
Hmph. At his level, it's not 
even worth remarking upon.

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:52.970
Jeez, you oughta at least 
be happy when you win.

00:19:52.970 --> 00:19:54.520
Don't even bother!

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:55.000
Huh?

00:19:55.450 --> 00:19:57.260
That's the kind of guy he is.

00:19:57.260 --> 00:20:01.230
Besides, can you imagine 
Kai smiling with delight?

00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:02.480
Mmm...

00:20:02.480 --> 00:20:04.070
Hmm...

00:20:04.070 --> 00:20:05.050
Well...

00:20:05.250 --> 00:20:06.980
Imagine, imagine...

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:08.930
II, yo...

00:20:12.580 --> 00:20:13.650
Impossible!

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:14.560
Right?!

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:19.120
Congratulations, Team Q4!

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:21.150
You trounced us!

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:23.140
You guys are strong!

00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:25.210
Yeah, you beat us good.

00:20:25.210 --> 00:20:27.180
Um...

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:28.910
Who the hell are you guys?!

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:30.910
How cruel! It's us!

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:31.770
Look!

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:35.120
Are you saying you've forgotten us?

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:37.000
Whaaat?!

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:38.900
Th-They're...

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:40.960
Not dark at all...

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:44.200
Were they actually white magicians?!

00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:47.710
Huh?

00:20:47.710 --> 00:20:49.240
Ahhhh!

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:51.520
Look at those names!

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:52.380
Huh?

00:20:53.090 --> 00:20:54.790
Hikaru Kurosawa...
(Note: Hikaru = to shine)

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:56.230
Laito Kuosaki...
(Note: Laito = light)

00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:57.740
Akira Kuroda?
(Note: Akira = light)

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:00.890
Their last names all have "dark" in them...

00:21:01.500 --> 00:21:03.740
...but every one of their first names...

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:05.820
is unbearably bright!

00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:11.020
Since they've got this second common point, 
why'd they have to go with the "dark side"?!

00:21:11.020 --> 00:21:12.170
It was fun!

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:13.640
We're gonna get going!

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:14.660
'Scuse us!

00:21:14.880 --> 00:21:17.790
Hold it!

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:20.580
You haven't fought the third matchup yet!

00:21:20.580 --> 00:21:24.520
I'm gonna beat you to make the score 3-0!

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:27.660
Didn't you know?

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:29.000
Know what?!

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:33.890
In this team competition, the team that wins the 
first two automatically advances to the next round.

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:39.100
In this case, you guys beat us twice 
in a row, so you're bumped up already.

00:21:39.100 --> 00:21:41.290
There is no third matchup.

00:21:41.290 --> 00:21:43.590
W-What?!

00:21:43.590 --> 00:21:46.100
It's true. It says it right here.

00:21:46.100 --> 00:21:50.080
Sorry. I should've checked beforehand...

00:21:51.970 --> 00:21:54.600
Kamui the Great didn't know...

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:55.990
DK, yo!

00:21:55.990 --> 00:21:57.880
He's a little too slow to catch on!

00:21:58.490 --> 00:22:00.750
N-Noooo...

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:04.640
Bye, Kamui. I look forward 
to fighting you someday.

00:22:04.640 --> 00:22:05.420
Yeah!

00:22:05.420 --> 00:22:06.620
Me too!

00:22:14.560 --> 00:22:17.970
Let me fight, too!

00:23:51.100 --> 00:23:52.900
That was nerve-wracking!

00:23:52.900 --> 00:23:54.580
I'm glad I somehow managed 
to pull a win out of it.

00:23:54.580 --> 00:23:57.360
You're lucky you were able 
to fight, Brother Aichi.

00:23:57.360 --> 00:24:00.060
But my heart was pounding, my knees were 
shaking, and I'm completely exhausted.

00:24:00.060 --> 00:24:01.940
Even so, you got to fight...

00:24:02.730 --> 00:24:05.960
What should I do when I'm all fired 
up like this, with nowhere to go?!

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:09.140
Don't worry! Next time, 
you'll take center stage!

00:24:09.140 --> 00:24:11.470
Next time: White Hot Tournament!

00:24:11.470 --> 00:24:14.550
Wow. I'm learning just by 
watching other teams fight.

00:24:14.550 --> 00:24:16.590
All of their images clashing,

00:24:16.590 --> 00:24:17.510
getting bigger and bigger...

00:24:17.510 --> 00:24:19.130
It's fun just watching!
